      a: "H3: higher conscientiousness goes with more perceived control. Supported. In the ordinal logistic on control, conscientiousness had B = -.349, p = .009, odds ratio about .71. Control was coded 1 = complete to 4 = none, so a negative B means more conscientious people were less likely to land in the low-control categories. In other words, more control.",
